<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- The Dead/Pass off-ramp. Declarative Screen Flow, not the LWC-ScreenAction shape the other
         Opportunity stage actions use (StageAdvanceController/StageAdvanceService), because
         Opportunity.StageName carries NO field-level-security grant anywhere in this org (zero
         permission sets, and every DPEG persona is on Minimum Access) - confirmed by a repo-wide
         sweep. The Apex path writes it with a bare `update o;`, which does not enforce FLS; an
         LDS-backed "Update a Record" quick action or a plain record-edit-form DOES enforce FLS and
         would silently drop the StageName write for every user (see ".claude" memory:
         "LDS form drops non-editable fields silently"). A Screen Flow run in System Context WITH
         SHARING gets the same FLS bypass the Apex path relies on, without needing new Apex or a new
         LWC bundle - `runInMode=SystemModeWithSharing` on Opportunity_Mark_Dead.flow-meta.xml.
         Sharing is deliberately still enforced (unlike this repo's SystemModeWithoutSharing
         background-automation flows) because this is a user-initiated write, not an automation
         read, and it must not let a deal driver touch a deal they cannot already see.

         AUTHORIZATION PARITY WITH THE OTHER EIGHT: the flow's first element is a Decision on
         {!$Permission.Acquisition_Deal_Actions}, matching the same server-side-first ordering
         StageAdvanceController documents ("PERMISSION (server-side, first statement in every
         method)"). The FlexiPage visibility rule on Opportunity_Record_Page asks the identical
         question for the button chrome, so the two halves agree by construction, the same
         relationship the other eight actions already have between their visibility rule and
         OpportunityActionPermissionService.assertDealActionAccess().

         StageName is written as the DECODED literal 'Dead/Pass' - the %2F-encoded form only ever
         appears in businessProcesses/recordTypes metadata, never at runtime (StageAdvanceService.cls
         :99-101). Rejection_Reason__c and StageName are written in ONE recordUpdates element so the
         Rejection_Reason_Required_On_Dead validation rule always sees a populated reason - there is
         no intermediate save that could strand a reason on a live deal. -->
    <flowDefinition>Opportunity_Mark_Dead</flowDefinition>
    <label>Mark Dead / Pass</label>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>Flow</type>
</QuickAction>
